\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces The classical flexible-job-shop picture. Solid arcs are the route of one school-bag order. Dashed arcs are a machine assignment. Operators, dies, thread lots, colour setups, and machine health are not nodes in this graph.}}{11}{figure.caption.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.2}{\ignorespaces The twin loop required by a status-aware schedule. The return arrow is the part most digital-twin case studies leave as a manual action by the planner.}}{19}{figure.caption.7}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.3}{\ignorespaces Route of one classic school backpack. Trolley bags and sports sacks use shorter or longer chains on the same cells. Cutting and colour-sensitive sewing are the steps that seize a shared token.}}{24}{figure.caption.8}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces One-hop heterogeneous graph of a single candidate bundle. The full shop graph is the union of these candidate graphs at the current ready set. Attention pools the four nodes; it does not mix two candidates before the scores are compared.}}{34}{figure.caption.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.2}{\ignorespaces Coupling of SSDT-CC into RCH-GAT. The score never reads a raw sensor. It reads a health state that maintenance and ordinary wear both rewrite.}}{49}{figure.caption.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.3}{\ignorespaces Health of Cutter-A at the start of three identical shell cuts. The renewed path begins after Equation~\eqref {eq:pm-map}. Neither path is a failure time. Both are the state the next score will read.}}{52}{figure.caption.14}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Executable architecture. The policy reads the twin and writes one bundle back into the cell. The KPI log is the only path from a run to the tables in Section~\ref {sec:estimate}.}}{60}{figure.caption.16}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Identification of the twenty score coefficients. The vertical axis is the preference-weighted cost divided, term by term, by first-in-first-out on the same training books. The search was stopped at generation 27. The coefficient vector used in the tables is the best vector observed, at \(0.366\).}}{63}{figure.caption.19}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.3}{\ignorespaces Nominal means rescaled onto one axis. Energy is multiplied by five and expected failures by fifty, so that a kilowatt-hour and a failure can sit beside a minute of makespan. The scaling is only for the drawing. Table~\ref {tab:nominal} has the unscaled numbers.}}{66}{figure.caption.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.4}{\ignorespaces Expected failures against the chance-constraint tolerance on the eight-book wear sweep. Loosening the veto lets the worn machines run and the failure count returns.}}{70}{figure.caption.26}%
